      <div type="clause" n="62">
        <head>Ine Rb 62</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="62" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="24" ed="#liebermann"/>CVI. Be þon þe mon to ceape<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.dagger"/> fordræfe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.18"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="62" corresp="#wit-g-prol"><pb n="24" ed="#liebermann"/>CVI. Be ðan þe man to ceace fordræfe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="62" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="25" ed="#liebermann"/>CVI. Be ðon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.7"/> ðe mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.2"/> to ceace fordræfe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="62" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="25" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.32"/> quis ad ceace pertrahatur, id est contamen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.33"/> uel fauces uel anclidiam.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.34"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="214" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>CVI Be þon þe mon to ceape fordræfe</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="214" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Be þam þe man to ceace fordræfe</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="25" ed="#liebermann"/>Darüber<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.de.1"/>, dass man zu Kessel[fang]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.de.2"/> treibt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Concerning someone being driven to the cauldron[-ordeal].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="215" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning when a man is driven <hi rend="italic">to</hi> <hi rend="italic">ceape</hi></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="215" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning when a man is driven <hi rend="italic">to ceace</hi></ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">24</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> ceace <hi rend="italic">aus G H B Quadr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read ceace, from G H B Quadr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">24</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-drife <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-drife So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">25</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Si quis accusatus transierit in manus redimentis et iterum delinquat <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>; De accusato pro delicto et i. fuit accusatus <hi rend="italic">Br statt Rb.</hi> 62</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Si quis accusatus transierit in manus redimentis et iterum delinquat Hk; De accusato pro delicto et i. fuit accusatus Br instead of Rb. 62</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">25</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">certamen <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">certamen T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">25</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ancillam <hi rend="italic">T</hi>; aneidiam <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ancillam T; aneidiam Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">25</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> ðam</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to ðam</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">25</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘demjenigen, welchen’ Schmid zwar grammatisch möglich, allein <hi rend="italic">be þon þe</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb: be</hi> II 1a) bildet Einen Begriff: ‘wenn’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘the one whom’ (Schmid) is grammatically possible, it is true, but <hi rend="italic">be þon þe</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb: be</hi> II 1a) forms a single concept: ‘if’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Ine_62.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">42</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hier weicht E, dem Frühere folgen, vom Archetyp, dessen <hi rend="italic">ceác</hi> (Kessel) die übrigen erhalten, ab; <hi rend="italic">s. u.</hi> zu Ine 37. 62. Im Q ist <hi rend="italic">contamen</hi> wohl nicht eine falsche Bildung für ‘Schande’, sondern Q’s Texte gemäss zu bessern in <hi rend="italic">certamen</hi>, wie eine gute Hs. liest. Dies aber meint wahrscheinlich nicht Ines richtigen Sinn ‘Gottesurteil’, sondern übersetzt verlesenes <hi rend="italic">cease</hi>. Durch <hi rend="italic">faux</hi> wird das hier nicht hergehörige Wort gleicher Buchstaben, das ‘Backen’ bedeutet (<hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Af 50), glossiert; Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Mittelengl. Wb.</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">cheke</hi>. Das hier ebenfalls sinnlose <hi rend="italic">anclidia</hi> ‘Schöpfrad’ (bei Ducange) stand vermutlich in einem Glossar zu <hi rend="italic">ceác</hi>; denn <hi rend="italic">antulum</hi> (-<hi rend="italic">us</hi>) steht in erhaltenen Glossaren für <hi rend="italic">ceac</hi>(<hi rend="italic">bora</hi>); Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Here E, whom earlier editors follow, departs from the archetype, whose <hi rend="italic">ceác</hi> (cauldron) the others preserve; <hi rend="italic">see below</hi> on Ine 37. 62. In Q, <hi rend="italic">contamen</hi> is probably not a false formation for ‘disgrace’ but is to be corrected, in accordance with Q’s text, to <hi rend="italic">certamen</hi>, as a good MS reads. This, however, probably does not mean Ine’s true sense, ‘ordeal’, but translates a misread <hi rend="italic">cease</hi>. <hi rend="italic">faux</hi> glosses the word of the same letters meaning ‘cheeks’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> Af 50), which does not belong here; Mätzner <hi rend="italic">Mittelengl. Wb.</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">cheke</hi>. The <hi rend="italic">anclidia</hi> ‘water-wheel’ (in Ducange), equally meaningless here, presumably stood in a glossary for <hi rend="italic">ceác</hi>; for <hi rend="italic">antulum</hi> (-<hi rend="italic">us</hi>) stands for <hi rend="italic">ceac</hi>(<hi rend="italic">bora</hi>) in extant glossaries; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
